lign="right">357</td><td align="right">150</td><td align="right">48</td><td align="right">1296</td><td align="right">171</td><td align="right">194</td><td align="right">174</td><td align="right">59</td><td align="right">3155</td><td align="right">3</td><td align="right">0</td><td align="right">1,022</td><td align="right">364</td><td align="right">29</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup>1</sup>See Table 1 for explanation of ICD-8 Chapters I-XVIII.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><p>Table <xref ref-type="table" rid="T3">3</xref> presents distribution of the number of sick-leave periods in each ICD-8 chapter for each of the 12 subjects who had had nine, ten, or eleven different sick-leave diagnoses. Among those individuals, besides musculoskeletal disorders, respiratory diseases and symptoms, the most common sick-leave diagnoses were in the category of symptoms, signs and ill-defined conditions (Chapter XVI).</p><table-wrap position="float" id="T3"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Distribution of sick-leave periods in each diagnostic category shown for persons who have had nine, ten, or eleven different sick-leave diagnoses</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td align="center" colspan="18"><bold>Number of sick-leave periods within each diagnostic category (ICD-8 Chapters I-XVIII)<sup>1</sup></bold></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td colspan="18"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>Number of sick-leave diagnoses</bold></td><td align="left">Subjects</td><td align="center">I</td><td align="center">II</td><td align="center">III</td><td align="center">IV</td><td align="center">V</td><td align="center">VI</td><td align="center">VII</td><td align="center">VIII</td><td align="center">IX</td><td align="center">X</td><td align="center">XI</td><td align="center">XII</td><td align="center">XIII</td><td align="center">XIV</td><td align="center">XV</td><td align="center">XVI</td><td align="center">XVII</td><td ali